  "body": "This came up recently while discussing the integration of sQUlearn into the AutoQML lib. Basically we need to remove any references to `num_features` in the standard workflow for the high level methods.\r\n\r\n## Status Quo\r\nCurrently we require `num_features` in the initialization of the encoding circuit which is itself required in the creation of the high level method.\r\n```python\r\nencoding_circuit = EncodingCircuit(\r\n    ...,\r\n    num_features=...\r\n    ...\r\n)\r\n...\r\nclf = QuantumClassifier(\r\n    ...,\r\n    encoding_circuit=encoding_circuit,\r\n    ...\r\n)\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Desired\r\nThis is not really good etiquette and we want to remove the need to know `num_features` in the instantiation of the high level method. Instead we want to use the dimension that is implicitly provided by `X` in the call to the `fit` method.",
